( lib/font.ux — 8x8 1bpp text over a game-declared Screen device.
  Import your devices file FIRST, then this library (screen helpers
  come along transitively):
      import "devices.ux"
      import "../lib/font.ux"
  `font8x8` holds printable ASCII 32-126 (95 glyphs x 8 rows,
  MSB-first, 760 bytes — the import cost). `draw_char` blits one
  glyph, `draw_string` walks a NUL-terminated string (literal or
  buffer) with `\n` newlines; anything outside 32-126 clamps to `?`
  via `glyph_clamp`. Device-touching helpers are MACROS, pure
  address math are fns (see `glyph_addr`, gated in test_font). )

import "screen.ux"

